V) Project 5: VisionAI – Computer Vision Intelligence
1. Problem statement
An image classification system that uses Convolutional Neural Networks to identify and classify images.
2. Flow
Input image -> preprocessing -> CNN model (convolution-ReLu-Pooling) -> Flatten+dense layer -> Prediction -> FastAPI -> React -> PostGre SQL
3. Explain CNN
A Convolutional Neural Network is a deep learning architecture primarily used for image-related tasks.
Layer	Purpose
Input	Receives image pixels
Convolution	Extracts image features
ReLU	Introduces non-linearity
Pooling	Reduces spatial dimensions
Flatten	Converts feature maps into a vector
Dense	Performs classification
Softmax	Produces class probabilities
4. Code
-> CNN
import tensorflow as tf
from tensorflow.keras import layers, models

model = models.Sequential([
    layers.Input(shape=(128, 128, 3)),

    layers.Conv2D(
        32, (3, 3), activation='relu'
    ),

    layers.MaxPooling2D((2, 2)),

    layers.Conv2D(
        64, (3, 3), activation='relu'
    ),

    layers.MaxPooling2D((2, 2)),

    layers.Flatten(),

    layers.Dense(128, activation='relu'),

    layers.Dense(5, activation='softmax')
])

